Z||000000||FieroKyle||09-25-2001||11:04 PM||||What did stock 95' Mustang GTs run on the quarter mile with the V-6 w/ automatic tranny??? Got a kid at school who is talking sh#t about my fiero.<P>85' GT, manual tranny, stock, except with no cat convert (&lt;---  big deal, lol  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P>Just seeing my chances here, weighing the possiblities.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||sqoach||09-25-2001||11:28 PM||||If that mustang's really a GT, then it has the V8. He'll win.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">           <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD(?)*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||09-25-2001||11:36 PM||||You would beat a v6 Mustang.<P>As for a 95 , 5.0ltr..Well , just so happens there's one in my garage , an auto none the less  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> but still a 5.0.<BR>It's slow... Sounds good , but slow , I would say a mid 15 sec car. They have terrible 2.78(?) gears in them. I raced a late 90's Lincoln Mark 8 last week and got beat. neck and neck to about 75mph , then his 300hp 4 cam 4.6ltr pulled away hard.<P>I think Low 15 sec , still faster on paper than any production Fiero. If it's a v6 Race him , if it's a 95 , 5.0ltr GT be careful.<P>Your gearing with the 4spd is an asset , as is your short 14" tires which makes for an even deeper gearset , but if the drag race is long he is going to beat you. 3rd gear with a 4spd tranny feels like an overdrive (spaced to far from 2nd)<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Brandon86SE||09-26-2001||12:03 AM||||It just so happens that I rent room and board from a guy who drives a 1995 Mustang GT.  (By the way, if it's a GT, then it has a 5.0, last year of the 5.0 by the way).  But ya, I've had the occasion to drive his car often enough, and it's pretty quick, and sounds real throaty, but I'd say it's no faster than my car in the 1/4.  (I ran a 15.3)  I know it will go faster than me in a all out down the freeway race, but in the 1/4 the weight difference would keep it even.  The big problem for him in the 1/4 is that there's no weight over his drive wheels!  On the track the typical 5.0 would probably spin more on launch than you would.  I'd say go for it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula||09-26-2001||01:31 PM||||I beat a 2001 Mustang GT 5 speed fairly easy....  <P><BR>Stroke This!!<P><BR>Go For It..... if he said it has a V6 then its not a GT... and a v6 fiero will smoke a V6 stang from that era, but my Formula Stock would only run side by side with a V6 2000 stang. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Formulasigs.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||09-26-2001||02:47 PM||||send him my way... i'll set him straight...<P>if it's a V8 you'll be hard pressed to keep up past the 1/8th... and in the 1.4 you'll just be sucking wind. sorry... if he just want to run 500' you'll destroy him, if both of you are running radials... he'll go up in smoke your be 3 cars in front of him. <P>------------------<BR>0-60 in 4.91||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroKyle||09-26-2001||10:05 PM||||Alright, well, its a V-6 and a GT, I looked at his car in the parking lot, I am guessing it is 95' could be 96' even, so I was giving a guess on the year. It has the body style after the 80's and early 90's.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula||09-26-2001||10:30 PM||||so its a V-6 that he put GT badges on?<P>if it has 1 exhaust pipe in the back its a 6 and if it has 2 then its an 8... unless he put dual exhaust on a 6, then oyu wont know until he pops the hood.<P>The whole concept of the GT is that it has a V8.  There shouldnt be any special V6 GTs out there because that would be a kick in the pants to ford.  <P>My guess is that its a V6 that he put GT badges on (cough cough rice cough).<P>But, if it says GT, has factory looking dual exhaust, rumbles, then its the real deal 5.0 liter V8 &lt;and it will RUMBLE&gt;.... If it looks like an aftermarket exhaust if it isnt rumbling a lot then its probably a 6. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroKyle||09-27-2001||11:02 PM||||May be is lieing to me, just starting to get a whiff of it. Trying to get me to race so I would lose and look stupid. Dual exhaust, GT badges, has a rumble thats very similar to my Fiero. Yup, time to ask him to open up the hood. I feel like there is a 5.0 slow hidden underneath.||||reg||1
