Z||000010||FieroKyle||09-28-2001||10:40 PM||||Alright today was race day. Good news and bad news. Bad news, right before the race, I found he actually has the 95' 5.0 with a 5-speed manual. Alright so we line up to race.....<P>The Pros, and Cons.<BR>Con- Engine difference<BR>Con- He has 5-speed manual<BR>Con- I only have 2 guys there to back up my little car in pre race (both had rode in the car before and telling everybody the Fiero is the sleeper)<BR>Con- Did I say engine difference???<BR>Pro- lighter car than Mudstain.<P><BR>We start out dead even and continue to do so until the 1/8th mark, he then begins to pull away, gets me by 1 car length. Fiero still running good, so i decide to give it one more shot. <P>We start and I have a half car length on him and gained a bit until once again the 1/8 th mark, then he pulls to a 3/4 car length on me to win both races. Really close still though.<P>Conclusion, before race time, we scheduled it an hour before. 24 people show up to watch it. All their jaws dropped as I was able to not only keep up, but come so close with a stock, naturally aspierate yada yada yada 2.8 V-6 while he had a 5.0 V-8 on the first run. Before we started he was so sure he was gonna kick my ass to hell and back and I would look like a fool. After those two runs, everyone gained total repsect for the little guy all wanted to see what this car was all about. Checking it out left and right, nobody went to go see the Mustang. Not only do I get better gas millage, better looks, but on top of this mudstain it has 10 more years of wear plus 118k miles compared to 65k and kept up. I was impressed a bit myself, excuse me while I have this big head for the time being.<P>The bad, after that 2nd run, the engine went doggy, and was not running the greatest. Both runs I went about 5500 to 6 grand rpms on every shift. I think I just added 20 years to the car in 30 seconds. I did have an exhaust leak, now its worse, I think the engine might be missing, so I am gonna check spark plugs and see what my dad thinks of it. I just drove the car tonight again and its back to its usual peppy self (most of the time), but the exhaust is leaking bad, so it sounds like a backfire. But, however I don't hear the engine missing at all so thats a plus. Anyways i will keep updates if anything further shows up.||||reg||4
Z||000011||FieroKyle||09-30-2001||12:19 AM||||bump||||reg||1
